Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:59:56 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Pair via secure-join QR instead of a typed address

Chatmail requires end-to-end encryption, so typing the peer's address could never pair. The setup screen now scans the assistant's secure-join invite QR (zxing-android-embedded, Apache-2.0, see THIRD-PARTY.md) or accepts the pasted QR text as a fallback, and completes the handshake through dc_transport.complete_pairing; the returned peer address is what gets stored. recordPairedPeer is split out so the Kotlin/module contract is unit tested (Robolectric).
